# Cases are CONSTRUCTED, never committed. Every artifact under case/ is a pure
# function of the builder in `build_battery_case.jl` plus its recorded seeds, so
# committing it would ship a second, drifting source of truth for the case.
# The manifest hashes belong in the phase record, not in git.
case/

# SDDP.jl writes these into the working directory when a node fails: the whole
# subproblem in MathOptFormat and the cuts it carried. They are debugging
# evidence for one run — megabytes each — and are regenerated by rerunning it.
subproblem_*.mof.json
model_infeasible_*.cuts.json
SDDP.log

# Figures written by the `plot_*` helpers in `battery_analysis.jl`. Their paths
# are chosen by the caller — the README's `value_curves.png` and `energy.png`
# are only examples — so the name cannot be enumerated. Scoped to this example
# directory, which tracks no image of its own.
*.png
